#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:194
msgid "WebGPU Runtime Loading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:196
msgid ""
"VTK's WebGPU module resolves a WebGPU implementation library at runtime "
"through a proc table. The eventual goal is to decouple the compile-time and "
"runtime dependencies so that the same VTK build works with different native "
"WebGPU runtimes (Dawn, wgpu-native) or browser WebGPU via Emscripten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:202
msgid ""
"This decoupling is not complete. When Dawn is found at configure time the "
"module links no implementation: the `wgpu*` names are redirected to a "
"dispatch table that the proc table fills in, so the only requirement is that "
"an implementation can be found at runtime. `vtkWebGPUConfiguration::"
"Initialize()` fails with a diagnostic if none can be."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:209
msgid ""
"On Emscripten there is no library to resolve: `--use-port=emdawnwebgpu` "
"links the implementation into the module, so the proc table reports itself "
"loaded without opening anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:213
msgid ""
"The implementation uses *lazy initialization* that is thread-safe and loads "
"on first access. The library is opened with global symbol visibility, so "
"direct calls to the WebGPU C API resolve against it without modification. "
"Missing libraries are reported at initialization (not link time), with clear "
"diagnostic messages. If functions are unavailable, wrappers return safe "
"values for graceful fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:220
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:222
msgid "The implementation consists of two layers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:224
msgid ""
"**vtkWebGPUProcTable** (C interface): loads the WebGPU implementation "
"library and resolves function pointers using the runtime's proc address "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:227
msgid ""
"**vtkWebGPUProcLoader** (C++ singleton, internal): wraps the proc table with "
"lazy initialization. Provides `IsLoaded()` and `Load()`, and is reached "
"through `vtkWebGPUConfiguration::Initialize()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:231
msgid ""
"VTK's sources call the WebGPU C API by its ordinary names. The build forces "
"`Private/vtkWebGPUProcDispatch.h` into the module's own sources and its "
"tests, and that header `#define`s each `wgpu*` name to the matching entry in "
"a table of function pointers, filled in from `wgpuGetProcAddress` once the "
"library is open. The forced include keeps the redirect off installed headers "
"and out of anything a consumer compiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:238
msgid ""
"`Private/vtkWebGPUProcDispatch.{h,cxx}` are generated. After updating "
"`ThirdParty/webgpuheaders`, regenerate them and commit the result:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:241
msgid "python3 Rendering/WebGPU/generate_proc_dispatch.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:245
msgid ""
"Handles cannot take the entry points as template arguments any more - the "
"address of a table entry is not a constant expression - so `vtkWebGPU::"
"Handle` takes a traits type whose `AddRef`/`Release` call through the table "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:249
msgid ""
"Initialization flow: `vtkWebGPUConfiguration::Initialize()` invokes "
"`vtkWebGPUProcLoader::GetInstance()`, which loads the WebGPU implementation "
"library (e.g., `libwgpu_dawn.so`), resolves function pointers via the proc "
"table, then creates a WebGPU adapter and device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:254
msgid "Standard WebGPU Headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:256
msgid ""
"VTK vendors a copy of the upstream [webgpu-headers](https://github.com/"
"webgpu-native/webgpu-headers) C API in `ThirdParty/webgpuheaders`. It "
"defines the core WebGPU types (`WGPUInstance`, `WGPUDevice`, etc.) and the "
"function signatures that the proc table resolves at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:262
msgid ""
"This vendored copy is what VTK compiles against on *every* platform, "
"including builds that link Dawn — `VTK::webgpuheaders` is a public "
"dependency, so its include directory is searched ahead of any "
"implementation's. VTK is therefore decoupled from a particular "
"implementation at the header level: the API cannot change underneath VTK, "
"and downstream consumers resolve the same header through `find_package(VTK)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:269
msgid ""
"Both VTK's public headers and its implementation files use the C API only. "
"No C++ wrapper (`webgpu_cpp.h`) is vendored or included; ownership of the C "
"handles is expressed with `Private/vtkWebGPUHandle.h`. The module builds as "
"C++17 and the installed interface does not require C++20 of its consumers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:274
msgid ""
"Upstream deliberately declares only the standard API. Implementations extend "
"it through `nextInChain`, using `WGPUSType` values from blocks upstream "
"reserves for them. The two extensions VTK uses — Dawn's adapter power "
"preference and emdawnwebgpu's canvas selector — are declared in `Private/"
"vtkWebGPUImplExtensions.h`, each behind the compile-time flag for the "
"implementation that provides it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:281
msgid "Library Search Strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:283
msgid ""
"If an explicit library path is given to the loader, it is tried first and on "
"its own. Otherwise the proc table tries the following names, in this order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:286
msgid "`libwgpu_dawn.so` (the default when no path is supplied)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:287
msgid "`libwebgpu_dawn.so`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:288
msgid "`libwgpu_dawn.so.0` (versioned variant)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:289
msgid "`libwebgpu_dawn.so.0` (versioned variant)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:290
msgid "`libwgpu_dawn.dylib` (macOS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:291
msgid "`libwebgpu_dawn.dylib` (macOS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:292
msgid "`wgpu_dawn.dll` (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:293
msgid "`webgpu_dawn.dll` (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:295
msgid ""
"An explicit path is opened through `vtkDynamicLoader` on every platform. A "
"bare name is opened with `LoadLibraryW` on Windows, so that the standard DLL "
"search order applies: `vtkDynamicLoader` routes a name through `Encoding::"
"ToWindowsExtendedPath`, which resolves it against the current working "
"directory instead of searching `PATH`. Elsewhere `vtkDynamicLoader` maps "
"onto `dlopen`/`dlsym`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:302
msgid ""
"**Custom paths**: You can override the search by setting environment "
"variables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:303
msgid "Linux: `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/path/to/lib`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:304
msgid "macOS: `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/path/to/lib`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:305
msgid "Windows: `PATH=\\path\\to\\lib`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:307
msgid ""
"Or by naming the library outright: set `VTK_WEBGPU_LIBRARY` to the path of "
"the implementation to load, and the search above is skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:310
msgid "Debugging and Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:312
msgid "**Library loading failed:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:313
msgid ""
"Check if the WebGPU library is installed: `ldconfig -p | grep -E '(wgpu_dawn|"
"webgpu_dawn)'` (Linux), or verify in `/usr/lib` or `/opt/local/lib` (macOS), "
"or `PATH` (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:316
msgid ""
"Ensure the library is in a standard search path or set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/"
"path/to/lib` (Linux), `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` (macOS), or `PATH` (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:319
msgid ""
"Test library loading directly: `python3 -c \"import ctypes; ctypes.CDLL('/"
"path/to/libwgpu_dawn.so')\"` (adjust path/name as needed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:322
msgid "**Function not found:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:323
msgid ""
"Verify the function name is spelled correctly and the length is correct "
"(must match string length in bytes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:325
msgid ""
"Check if the loaded library version exports the function: `nm /usr/lib/"
"libwgpu_dawn.so | grep wgpuFunctionName`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/README.md:327
msgid "Enable debug output in vtkWebGPUProcTable.cxx during development"
msgstr ""

